{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And Yitzchak loved Esav, because he had game in his mouth.</b> The verse explains that he did not love him on account of his firstborn status, but only because he gratified him with his hunting. And the verse teaches us that Esav the wicked was a hunter in two ways: he would hunt the animals in the wildernesses and in the fields, as indicated by 'a man of the field,' and he would also hunt the mind of his father, when he would prepare gratifications with his mouth, through the cunning of his words — and this is 'because he had game in his mouth.'" "<b>And our Rabbis of blessed memory said</b> in the Midrash: Esav the wicked would say to his father, 'Salt is liable for tithes,' and Yitzchak would be astonished and say, 'How scrupulous my son is in commandments!' He would say to him, 'My son, where were you today?' He would answer him, 'In the house of study, and I learned such-and-such a halakhah and such-and-such a matter.' And the holy spirit cries out and says, ״כי יחנן קולו אל תאמן בו כי שבע תועבות בלבו״ — 'when he graces with his voice, do not trust him, for seven abominations are in his heart.' And further they interpreted: he would hunt and feed his father, and give him a bribe, so that he might take the blessing. And this is what is written (Deuteronomy 16:19): ״כי השוחד יעור״ — 'for a bribe blinds,' etc. And of Yitzchak it is written: ״ותכהין עיניו מראות״ — 'and his eyes were dim from seeing' — end of quotation. And we see that just as Esav was a man of bribery, so we see his seed as recipients of bribes, lovers of gluttonous feeding, as he said, ״הלעיטני נא״ — 'feed me, I pray.' And of them David, peace be upon him, said (Psalms 108): ״מתרפס ברצי כסף״ — 'he cringes for handfuls of silver.' And they draw strength from the prince that is theirs, who receives bribes, in the house of, etc. And so every nation draws strength from the prince that is theirs. And you already know that from him the serpent received power to cause sin and to shed blood, and he was the father and root of all who choose blood and consume it. And he is the one who aids the seed of Esav the red to shed blood, and he is the accuser of Israel, who are circumcised and who distance themselves from eating blood. And to him the cunning accuser intended, who nullified the covenant of circumcision and permitted blood, because it fell to his lot — therefore they cling to him. And this is what the prophet said to the seed of Esav (Ezekiel 35:6): ״אם לא דם שנאת ודם יהדפך״ — 'Surely you hate blood, and blood shall pursue you.' He prophesies upon him destruction, because his hatred is the blood of circumcision. And this is what the verse says (Jeremiah 48:10): ״וארור מונע חרבו מדם״ — 'and cursed is he who withholds his sword from blood' — this is the blood of circumcision."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {1 "The abbreviation ביה\"כ is expanded as בית הכופר ('house of bribery') based on context; alternatively it could read בית הקדש ('the house of [the one who receives] bribery'), but the sense is the prince or angel who accepts bribes."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:15:18.120575809Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}